      "message": "feat(app,ui): lay the part on a plane through three picked points\n\nThree model corners span a plane laid on the setup's G17/G18/G19 plane\nthrough the face pick's own apply path (pick::plane::lay_datum), so a\nface and three corners of it give the same alignment. The outside is\nthe side away from the part's material; Flip turns it. Optional 3-2-1\nframe: point 1 to the origin, 1 -> 2 along +X (+Y for G19). One\nundoable AlignPartToSetup (lay_on_points / check_points); refusals by\nname: not three vertices, coincident (< 0.001 mm), (nearly) collinear\n(< 1 degree of spread), off the part, no model. Setup page row \"Lay on\na plane - pick three points\" with point prompts, Remove last, Clear\npoints and a greyed Apply with the reason; MCP tool lay_part_on_points.\n\nFixes #555\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
      "tree": {
