      },
      "message": "fix(ui): laying a picked face on a plane turns the part\n\nReproduced through the real Setups page at the 1280 x 720 hand-test\nwindow, the seed block turned 30 degrees about X. The turn itself was\nright all along (pick::lay_on_plane + AlignPartToSetup, on main too);\nwhat the user could reach was not:\n\n- On main the \"Lay on a plane\" row armed Edge mode, so a click on the\n  face took an edge and Apply stayed grey. #554 (7d641c8b, on this\n  stack) already arms Face mode.\n- The row was one long line, so Flip, \"Face to plane level\" and Apply\n  (placed after \"Picked: Face <19-digit id> of ...\") ran past the\n  properties pane's right edge, out of reach. The only Apply in reach\n  was the Part alignment row's (a typed turn about the bounds centre).\n\nThe face row now uses short lines and its own \"Apply face\" button on a\nline of its own; the three-points (#555) and axes-in-the-plane (#557)\nrows, which overflowed the same way, get short lines too.\n\nPinned by ui egui_app::tests::plane_face_lay (a real click on a tilted\nface, Flip, Apply face: the face ends -Z at Z 0 with the part above;\nCtrl+Z restores), structural::setup_page_alignment_rows_structure\n(every option of the three rows on screen) and app plane_align\na_tilted_face_is_turned_flat_onto_each_plane_with_the_part_above_it\n(G17/G18/G19 through the command, undo).\n\nFixes #330\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
