      "message": "feat(setups): part alignment turns about the WCS origin and lays the picked face down\n\nThe Setups page's Part alignment row's typed angles now turn the part\nabout the setup's WCS origin by default: the part's point on the origin\nstays there (the maintainer's \"it shifts the model relative to the\norigin\"). The row names its pivot in an \"about [WCS origin | part\ncentre]\" combo beside Apply, on a line of its own; \"part centre\" is\nthe old turn. The presets keep turning about the part's centre. One\nundoable AlignPartToSetup (new AlignPartToSetup::turn, app::setup_turn).\n\n\"Lay on a plane\" now lays a new pick face down: the face row's toggle\nis \"Face down\" and the points row's \"Points down\", both on by default.\nOnly the UI draft's default changed - PlaneLay::flip, the MCP tools\nand saved projects (which store the transform, not the flag) are\nuntouched.\n\nsetup_page_alignment_rows_structure asserts every alignment control\nlies inside the properties pane's rect, not just the window; it fails\non the #330 one-line regression.\n\nStacked on #603. Decisions: docs/decisions/606-align-pivot.md.\n\nFixes #606\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
